*Key Takeaways: CAICT has conducted some very intriguing tests on Chinese
AI models that have identified high safety/security risks, but most of the
reported results are anonymized.*

   -

   In July 2025, CAICT released safety/security evaluations of 15 models
   from three companies (2 from DeepSeek, 9 from Alibaba=E2=80=99s Qwen, 4 =
from
   Zhipu=E2=80=99s GLM). According to their classification framework, the r=
esults
   were: controllable risk - one model in this category, low risk - three
   models, medium risk - nine models, and high risk - two models. Below are
   the results on the different tests for the two high-risk models (Table 1=
):

<https://substack.com/redirect/24587b40-025d-4510-a78a-45a925a95713?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>
Source:
AI Safety/Security Research Report (CAICT, Nov 2025)

   -

   In that ChinAI #315 post, I wrongly determined that the CAICT AI safety
   benchmark=E2=80=99s scope had shrunk over time, with a lot of focus on
   hallucinations. I missed these detailed assessments of coding LLMs.

*A few other interesting results from the report:*

   -

   In a joint test of DeepSeek R1 (671B-parameter version), CAICT and Ant
   Group found that 6% of the model's reasoning processes involved sensitiv=
e
   categories, labeling this a =E2=80=9Cnew type of content security risk=
=E2=80=9D.
   -

   CAICT=E2=80=99s first batch of tests in 2024 studied models=E2=80=99 saf=
eguards against
   adversarial attacks such as prompt injections. Now, CAICT reports that =
=E2=80=9C*a
   domestic reasoning large model released in 2025 showed a 200% surge in
   harmful content output rates under inducement attacks*.=E2=80=9D
   -

   Another very noteworthy finding: a group of Peking University
   researchers discovered an =E2=80=9Cinfinite output=E2=80=9D vulnerabilit=
y in DeepSeek=E2=80=99s R1.
   The prompt, =E2=80=9CThe distance between two paths in a tree=E2=80=9D [=
=E6=A0=91=E4=B8=AD=E4=B8=A4=E6=9D=A1=E8=B7=AF=E5=BE=84=E4=B9=8B=E9=97=B4=E7=
=9A=84=E8=B7=9D=E7=A6=BB], would
   cause the model to be so deeply engrossed in its chain of thought reason=
ing
   that it could not stop. Here=E2=80=99s the relevant *anquan neican
   <https://substack.com/redirect/233df616-a831-4397-a4a6-2cfb85e0697d?j=3D=
eyJ1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>*
   (a Chinese platform that covers cybersecurity issues) coverage. The Peki=
ng
   study also found that random garbled characters could trigger the endles=
s
   reasoning.

